# What must never reach the build context.
#
# Two reasons, and the first one is the serious one: anything copied into an
# image is in the image for whoever ever pulls it. The .env holds Google
# passwords, TOTP secrets and the GeeLark key; the service-account JSON grants
# write access to the spreadsheet. Both are mounted at run time instead.
#
# The second is size. This runs on a 1 vCPU box, and every megabyte of context
# is read and sent to the daemon before the build starts.
.env
.env.*
secrets/
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json

# Run state and output. The ledger is mounted from a volume; artifacts and
# logs are written into ones. A copy of yesterday's baked into the image is
# confusing at best.
state/
artifacts/
logs/
*.log

# Local to a developer's machine.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Not .git: `--version` reads the commit out of it when there is one, and
# leaving it out is why GEELARK_REVISION exists. The build passes the answer
# in as an argument, so the history itself is not needed.
.git/
.github/
